oudini Game Environments | Procedural Environments\n EN Deep dive into Creating Assets and Architecture for Game Environments, from Maya and ZBrush to Unreal Engine 5.\n\nGiovani Magana's two-course series gave me a concrete framework for production-ready environment workflows: how to plan modularity, control silhouette at each LOD stage, and approach procedural generation with intent rather than chance.\n\nProcedural modeling HDA focusing on orientation and alignment. Houdini handles alignment through the normal attribute, no manual rotation needed. Quick variation of dimensions, material types, and ornamentation.\n FR Plongée dans Creating Assets and Architecture for Game Environments, de Maya et ZBrush à Unreal Engine 5.\n\nLa série de deux cours de Giovani Magana m'a donné un cadre concret pour des workflows d'environnement prêts pour la production : planifier la modularité, contrôler la silhouette à chaque étape de LOD, et aborder la génération procédurale avec intention.\n\nHDA de modélisation procédurale axé sur l'orientation et l'alignement. Houdini gère l'alignement via l'attribut normal, pas de rotation manuelle nécessaire. Variation rapide des dimensions, types de matériaux et ornementations.\n\n11 Niagara Vortex VFX | VFX / Grooming\n EN VFX project using Niagara and custom meshes to create magical vortex effects that respond to gameplay mechanics in real-time. Features interactive fur simulation, vortex forces, and stylized rendering techniques.\n FR Projet VFX utilisant Niagara et des meshes personnalisés pour créer des effets de vortex magiques répondant aux mécaniques de gameplay en temps réel. Comprend une simulation de fourrure interactive, des forces de vortex et des techniques de rendu stylisé.\n\n13 Procedural Rock Gen | Houdini Point VOP\n EN Rock sculpting workflow using Point VOP with controlled noise displacement. Pipeline: cube to VDB from poly to smooth to convert. Focuses on realistic weathering and surface detailing.\n FR Workflow de sculpture de rochers utilisant Point VOP avec déplacement de bruit contrôlé. Pipeline : cube vers VDB depuis poly vers lissage vers conversion. Se concentre sur l'érosion réaliste et les détails de surface.\n\n104 Ceramic Tiles - Made with Houdini Copernicus and Unreal Lumen | Houdini · Copernicus\n EN A ceramic tile material rebuilt inside Houdini's Copernicus after Julien Delannoy's Substance 3D Designer project, rendered in Unreal Engine 5.8 with Lumen.\n FR Un matériau de carreaux de céramique reconstruit dans Copernicus sous Houdini d'après le projet Substance 3D Designer de Julien Delannoy, rendu dans Unreal Engine 5.8 avec Lumen.\n\nzenray-progress-design-01 | ZenRayProgress, component by component | A tour of the design, screen by screen\n  P: ZenRayProgress gathers, in one place, the tools I use every day. The point was never to write one more app, but to bring together the ones I kept opening separately: a drive, a calendar, a timer, a notebook, a library, and to put them on a site I can reach from anywhere. One central space for everything I look up, keep and build.\n  P: The site first ran on Vercel, then on Cloudflare, on a free plan both times. That hosting detail is not the subject of this page. What follows is a tour of the design, screen by screen and component by component, to keep a record of how the interface looks at this date.\n\nzenrayprogress | ZenRayProgress | Every files, in a tab.\n  P: As a technical artist, I'm often confronted with vast numbers of software. I was dreaming about an app, like a drive, that could centralize my files and let me open and edit them.\n  P: I'm proud to have built something that gets close to my vision, but this is still a preview app that could be enhanced.\n\nzenray-dictate | ZenRay Dictate | ChatGPT dictation, everywhere on macOS.\n  P: A painter does not add paint to make something pretty. He adds colour to make something appear, or disappear. Code is the same. You need a function, you write it. You do not, you erase it.\n  P: I wanted dictation that actually works, everywhere on my machine, the way Parakeet or Wispr Flow do it. Those models still make plenty of mistakes in French and in Japanese, and the good ones are paid. So I took apart the single component I cared about in ChatGPT, the dictation, and gave it a window of its own. Fn brings up a small bar, Cmd+D starts and stops, the text lands on your clipboard. Fre\n\nmetahuman-markerless-macos | MetaHuman Animator Markerless Motion Capture Plugin on macOS | \n  P: What I aim for in this exercise. If you are already making mocap from live sessions, you know that taking the first animations out of your videos can be a pain to have something clean on the first passes. Take a movement that exists on a video and having it directly inside the game engine is what Unreal Epic Games' team of magicians solves! In this showcase, a four second attack animation from a g\n  P: Retarget onto SKM_Quinn, from video.\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3a3ab371-2230-4d92-b073-57f0da16eb28","timestamp":"2026-10-03T10:45:52.241Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"34 HDA Stairs Component | Houdini · Church\n EN A procedural staircase HDA built in Houdini for the Louisiana Bayou Church. 37 nodes, 3 exposed parameters: height, step count, tread depth. The graph handles stringers, treads, support pillars, ladder rails and rungs, with a mirror node for bilateral symmetry.\n FR Un HDA d'escalier procedural construit dans Houdini pour la Louisiana Bayou Church. 37 nodes, 3 parametres exposes : hauteur, nombre de marches, profondeur. Le graph gere limons, marches, piliers de soutien, rampes et barreaux, avec un node mirror pour la symetrie bilaterale.\n\n31 Procedural Shutters in Houdini | Houdini\n EN A procedural shutter asset built in Houdini as part of a larger procedural house system. Built on top of pre-existing geometry groups to avoid breaking the model, reusing what already exists rather than s