{"parentUuid":"ace20ab0-61f4-46cb-a094-a44eda4425de","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffAuqBCQQ2e4C5PSm8rR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0166S2Gvvu9FsfvdnexviYfm","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-cv-pdf/site && python3 - <<'EOF'\nbody=open('/tmp/cv_data_body.js',encoding='utf-8').read()\nbody=body.replace('const skills = [','export const skills = [').replace('const experiences = [','export const experiences = [').replace('const education = [','export const education = [')\nhead='''/* ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n   CV DATA, THE SINGLE SOURCE FOR THE CV PAGE AND THE CV PDF (3 October 2026)\n   FR : source unique du CV, lue par la page /cv ET par le générateur de PDF (scripts/cv/).\n\n   Isomorphic on purpose (3 October 2026): plain data and pure functions, no browser API, no JSON import,\n   so Vite (the page) and Node (the PDF builder) read exactly the same module.\n   FR : isomorphe volontairement, pour que la page et le PDF ne puissent jamais diverger.\n\n   Where each thing lives (3 October 2026):\n   - skills, experiences, education, labels : here, bilingual (EN first, FR second).\n   - projects : NOT here. They are generated from the real portfolio (PROJECTS in src/App.jsx) by\n     scripts/cv/build-cv-data.mjs into src/cv/cvProjects.generated.json, then merged with the curated short\n     blurbs of src/cv/cvProjectBlurbs.json by buildCvProjects() below. A project added to the site shows up\n     on the CV at the next build, and its link is the site's own route, never typed by hand.\n   ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */\n\nexport const CV_UPDATED = { en: 'October 2026', fr: 'Octobre 2026' }   // 3 October 2026\n\nexport const CV_IDENTITY = {                                            // 3 October 2026\n  name: 'M